From 892de7c08db49771ee65546e66d771c23acbc6d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MeetSweet Dev <meetsweet@volttaik.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:32:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Authoritative live role in auth; expose qualities on post
 detail and feed rows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- requireAuth/optionalAuth now re-read the account's role from the DB on every
  request instead of trusting the (possibly stale) JWT role claim. A user who
  becomes a creator after login is immediately authorized for creator-only
  endpoints (album creation, uploads) without waiting for a token refresh, and
  a demoted/deleted account loses access immediately. Fixes the recurring
  "Creator account required" regression for valid creators.
- POST detail + generic feed rows now include server-authoritative qualities
  (single Auto variant today) so the mobile player receives them on the content
  detail screen; locked content still returns [] so no media URL leaks.

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
